# superseded prototype snapshots kept locally for reference only
old/
old prototype/

# The brand source art — book, original fonts, logos, printables (~174MB).
# Untracked as of 2026-08-02: it was pushing the repo past GitHub's size
# limits (NameTag-70x100-3mmBleed.indd alone is 57MB, over the 50MB
# recommendation). It still lives on disk, and every version through
# commit 8739af2 remains in history — `git checkout 5a47349 -- Brand`
# brings any of it back.
# The site does NOT read from here: prototype/assets/ holds its own copies
# of the fonts, logos and the linen texture.
Brand/

# Real video trialled in the holders. 51.8 MB for one reel — past GitHub's
# 50 MB warning and into every clone forever, for an asset that belongs on
# R2 and is served by URL, not bundled. Same reasoning as Brand/ above.
prototype/media/

# fit_columns.py writes its screenshot to the CWD, so it lands at the repo
# root. It is a picture of a solve, not the solve — the numbers it produces
# go into style.css and that is what is kept.
why_fitted_*.png

# ⚠️ resources/ IS tracked — it holds the source art the derived assets come
# from — so anything large dropped in there goes straight into the repo and
# into every clone forever. Video does not belong in git at all: it lives on
# R2 and is served by URL. One 111 MB reel landed here on 2026-08-16 and would
# have been committed silently.
# The small green-screen clip the dropcap sprite is baked from predates this
# and is already tracked, so it is excluded from the rule by name.
resources/*.mp4
resources/*.mov
!resources/Paper Crumple Effect Green Screen.mp4

# Python bytecode from the resources/ build scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.gstack/
resources/shots/
resources/edge-cdp*/

# Derivative cache for thumb_media.py — pulled from R2 and re-derived on
# demand, so nothing here is a source.
resources/thumb-cache/

# Splice scripts write to a temp file beside their target and os.replace() it
# over the original — never opening the only copy for writing. A crash between
# mkstemp and replace leaves a zero-byte .tmp behind, and prototype/ is the
# DEPLOY DIRECTORY, so two of them shipped into a commit on 2026-08-27b.
*.tmp

# ── Google service-account keys ────────────────────────────────────
# 🔴 A downloaded service-account key is a PRIVATE KEY. Google names the
# file after the project (`my-project-4f3a91c2b7.json`), so it does not look
# like a credential in a directory listing, and it lands in ~/Downloads with a
# name nobody recognises a week later. These patterns are here so that dropping
# one into the tree to pipe into `wrangler secret put` cannot commit it.
#
# ⚠️ The secrets themselves live in Cloudflare, write-only. The downloaded JSON
# is the ONLY copy of the key that will ever exist -- keep it somewhere durable
# and OUTSIDE this repo. See feedback-worker/SETUP.md step 2.
# ⚠️ `*-*.json` is deliberately BROAD -- it catches any hyphenated .json,
# not only a key. That is the trade: no tracked file in this repo has a hyphen
# in its name, and a silently-ignored config is a cheaper mistake than a
# committed private key. `git add -f` if you ever need one through.
*-*.json
sa.json
service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*.pem
*.p12
